# Environment variable NAMES only — never values.
# TECHNICAL_ARCHITECTURE.md §18: "No secret ever enters Git. No secret ever reaches the browser."
# `.gitignore` already excludes `.env` and `.env.*` and allows only this file.
#
# These are the WEB APPLICATION's build-time variables. The Studio has its own, in
# studio/.env.example.

# --- CMS reads, build time only (§8, §18) ------------------------------------
# Public identifiers, not secrets. The dataset is private (§18.1), so reads need the token below.
SANITY_PROJECT_ID=
SANITY_DATASET=

# Read-only **Viewer** token. Set as an ENCRYPTED secret in the Cloudflare Pages build
# environment (§18) — never a plaintext variable, never in a Function, never in a client bundle.
#
# §18's consequence to respect: a Viewer token *can* read drafts, because narrower read roles
# are Enterprise-only. That is why the query layer pins `perspective: 'published'`, pins the API
# version, and fails the build on any `drafts.` id — three independent defences, all in
# src/lib/content/.
#
# An Editor/write token must exist NOWHERE in this system: not in CI, not in the frontend, not
# in a Function, not in the build.
SANITY_READ_TOKEN=

# --- Preview environment ONLY (§6.2, §18) ------------------------------------
# The draft-reading token. It exists only in the separate, Cloudflare Access-protected preview
# deployment, server-side. It must never be set in production or in CI.
# SANITY_PREVIEW_TOKEN=

# --- Contact Pages Function (§19.3) — not yet implemented --------------------
# Encrypted Pages Function secrets. Listed here so the names are agreed before the Function
# lands; setting them has no effect until then.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=
# CONTACT_INBOX=
